{
    "background_story": "Dahlia was a free-spirited artist, known for her unconventional approach to creativity. She spent most of her life feeling trapped by the conventions of traditional art forms. One day, while exploring an abandoned factory, Dahlia stumbled upon an old, rusty door with a sign that read 'Do Not Enter'. The sign became a challenge to her, and she felt an overwhelming urge to unbolt the door and unlock the secrets within. As she pushed the door open, a flood of light illuminated the space, revealing a treasure trove of discarded machinery and industrial artifacts. Dahlia saw beauty in the discarded and began to create stunning sculptures from the scrap metal. Her art studio, 'Unbolted', became a symbol of liberation, inspiring others to break free from the ordinary and unleash their creativity.",
